[{"_1":2},"routes/project",{"_3":4},"data",{"_5":6},"project",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26,"_27":28,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":42,"_43":44,"_45":46,"_47":48,"_49":50},"slug","cinebook","name","CineBook","kicker","One seat. One winning request.","number","02","description","A movie and event booking experience with temporary seat holds, fair waitlists, live inventory, and recovery when things go wrong.","categories",[75],"stack",[70,71,72,73,74],"image","/images/cinebook.webp","imageAlt","CineBook dark movie discovery interface","accent","mint","github","https://github.com/Mayank2142/ticket-booking","demo","https://ticket-booking-production-dd12.up.railway.app","featured",true,"kind","Full-stack project","role","Full-stack application development, booking workflows, API integration and reliability.","problem","A seat grid is straightforward until customers compete for one seat, abandon checkout, or accept a waitlist offer at the same moment.","solution","Model inventory per show, enforce ownership and expiry at the database boundary, and connect the interface to live invalidation and recoverable background work.","architecture",[65,66,67,68,69],"decisions",[54,55,56],"evidence",[51,52,53],"lessons","The happy path is only one part of a booking system. Ownership, expiry, cancellation and retries deserve the same design attention.","note","The demo uses sample events and no real payment gateway. Its documented deployment does not currently send external email. SQLite is available for local/test use.","Customer, organiser and administrator workflows","Committed screenshots across light and dark themes","Documented concurrency and recovery behavior",{"_57":63,"_59":64},{"_57":61,"_59":62},{"_57":58,"_59":60},"title","Keep the queue fair","text","A cancellation can become a single-use offer to the next eligible queue member instead of a free-for-all.","Recover abandoned work","Expiry is enforced during reads and by a background worker, with durable jobs for interrupted processing.","Make the database authoritative","Atomic state conditions validate the seat, hold owner and expiry before confirmation. UI state is not the booking lock.","React + TypeScript customer and operations UI","Node API and shared validation","PostgreSQL authoritative inventory","SSE + optional Redis invalidation","Durable expiry and notification jobs","React","TypeScript","Node.js","PostgreSQL","SSE","Full-stack"]
